  {
   "key": "0x00..0x7F",
   "name": "port C bit set/reset",
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
     "lines": "203-211"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
     "lines": "215-229"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
     "lines": "457-467"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
     "lines": "500-504"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/i8255.cpp",
     "function": "i8255_device::set_pc_bit"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/i8255.cpp",
     "function": "i8255_device::set_inte"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/i8255.cpp",
     "function": "i8255_device::set_inte1"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/i8255.cpp",
     "function": "i8255_device::set_inte2"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Any of the eight bits of port C can be set or reset with a single output instruction.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "203-207",
       "sha": "1d7d8a703bb6786fdbc59aa1c8c8ec4e45bbf0290c474a2a44c03ed70b25e89c"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "When port C is status/control for port A or B, its bits can be set or reset as if they were data output ports.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "208-211",
       "sha": "99ce8d2fadcf7ede21dc1a67c3bedb15ab3c03fb845b0c7cd9ddaf7cb81d372b"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The interrupt request signals of mode 1 and mode 2 are inhibited or enabled by setting or resetting the associated INTE flip-flop with the port C bit set/reset.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "215-222",
       "sha": "b2e1e7949ad1ef9067df1fde6a6529401291b3a9491ee5d8105f345978fb3fae"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Bit set/reset lets the programmer allow or disallow one I/O device to interrupt the CPU without affecting any other device in the interrupt structure.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "223-226",
       "sha": "8f565062671141da75d88b8c8033b7074bb756ce9bc0d9d39a6ba456cb130c8e"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Bit set sets the INTE flip-flop to enable interrupts; bit reset resets it to disable them.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "227-229",
       "sha": "16da93afcd20defa720cb12526fa97fee573ce4428dad663097d20f761c10201"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "6",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A port C line programmed as an output, INTR, IBF and OBF included, can be written by the command, or an interrupt enable flag set or reset.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "457-460",
       "sha": "c871efa890a3b4b05ee788110eb4b061a17beb85a3a234c56ec824de0ea1263f"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "7",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Port C lines programmed as inputs, ACK and STB included, are not affected; writing their bit positions changes the group A and B interrupt enable flags.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "460-467",
       "sha": "041ab233799bb20cfcb94216dd89ba8d565610eb0d32489127be3740fe2a29f8"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "8",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "INTE B is PC2, the pin of ACKB (output mode 1) or STBB (input mode 1).",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "501",
       "sha": "8cad3b787851e0ef770098de7a7d926ac911037ea09f4718f970f5cbabd5472d"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "9",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "INTE A2 is PC4, the pin of STBA (input mode 1 or mode 2).",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "502",
       "sha": "750412b03538e6c22e5bbaa86fe3a93ea4d134d39452b9ea7727de342cbe6a1e"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "10",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "INTE A1 is PC6, the pin of ACKA (output mode 1 or mode 2).",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82C55A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "503",
       "sha": "5c9fa44a7c1f083a547c14b8a5635d77f9c055f36bbec22c04d463b2ae513d1d"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
